[6.601554, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0m/tmp/uvv/bin/python -c \"import six; print('six (uv venv):', six.__version__)\"\r\nsix (uv venv): 1.17.0\r\n"]
[6.601617, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.830854, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mnode -e \"const isNumber = require('/tmp/npm-t/node_modules/is-number'); console.log('is-number:', isNumber(42), isNumber('abc'))\"\r\nis-number: true false\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.614767, "o", "All three installs succeeded, and each package imported once.\r\n\r\n1. **pip `--target`**: `python3 -m pip install --target /tmp/pip-t six` installed six 1.17.0. Import (with `PYTHONPATH=/tmp/pip-t`) printed: `six (pip --target): 1.17.0`\r\n2. **uv venv**: `uv venv /tmp/uvv` created the venv on CPython 3.12.3. Then `uv pip install --python /tmp/uvv/bin/python six` installed `six==1.17.0`. Import printed: `six (uv venv): 1.17.0`\r\n3. **npm**: `npm install --prefix /tmp/npm-t is-number` added 1 package. Import via `require` printed: `is-number: true false`\r\n\r\nThe `is-number` check called `isNumber(42)` and `isNumber('abc')`, which returned `true` and `false`.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
